        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Abraham Løkin\n- Places: Fuglafjørður, Faroe Islands, Norwegian Sea, North Atlantic, Norway, Iceland, Scotland\n- Organizations: ÍF Fuglafjørður\n- Roles: Football player, football manager\n- Topics: Faroe Islands geography, Faroese football\n\nFacts:\n- Abraham Løkin was born as Abraham Hansen on 16 June 1959 in Fuglafjørður in the Faroe Islands.\n- Abraham Løkin is a former Faroe Islands football player.\n- Abraham Løkin is a former manager of the Faroese football club ÍF Fuglafjørður.\n- The Faroe Islands are an archipelago between the Norwegian Sea and the North Atlantic.\n- The Faroe Islands lie about halfway between Norway and Iceland.\n- The Faroe Islands are about 200 miles north-northwest of Scotland.\n- The Faroe Islands are also sometimes called the Faeroe Islands.\n- The Faroese name of the Faroe Islands is Føroyar, and the Danish name is Færøerne.",
